# M0 exit transcript (ARCHITECTURE §22.2)

The five statements of `skeleton.in/skeleton.py` (both syntaxes mixed) produce one JSON
response per statement (§13.2 envelope). `skeleton.out/out/m0.glb` is the expected GLB,
byte for byte (its JSON and BIN chunks equal what Blender 5.2.4 writes for the same
scene, except `asset.generator`). `skeleton_stdin.toml` feeds the same statements on stdin.

```console
$ frap run skeleton.py
{"event":"ready","frap":"0.1.0","protocol":1,"blender_api":"5.2","startup":"factory"}
{"seq":1,"line":1,"kind":"op","op":"mesh.primitive_cube_add","ok":true,"status":"FINISHED","reports":[],"result":{"object":{"$ref":"bpy.data.objects['Cube.001']"}},"changes":{"added":["bpy.data.objects['Cube.001']","bpy.data.meshes['Cube.001']"],"removed":[],"modified":["bpy.data.collections['Collection']","bpy.data.scenes['Scene']"],"renamed":[]},"context":{"mode":"OBJECT","active_object":"Cube.001","selected_objects":["Cube.001"],"frame_current":1},"hints":[]}
